From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:35:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: let the nvram
 partition be written

The J604 marked its nvram partition read-only while the boot NOR
part was unconfirmed. The partition already matches the J604 entry in
spi-apple-qspi's board table (0x700000, 1 MiB), and the driver keeps
it read-only until root sets read_only=N, refuses any part whose JEDEC
ID it does not know, and bounds every program and erase to the
partition.

Drop read-only, so asahi-bless can set the boot volume from Linux.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 0f5bc0ffc9..85409af756 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -294,10 +294,6 @@ atcphy2_dp: endpoint {
 	};
 };
 
-&nvram {
-	read-only;
-};
-
 &ps_msg {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
-- 
2.43.0

